What:		/sys/devices/platform/.../gpu_power_ceiling
Date:		November 2026
Contact:		Asahi Linux contributors <asahi@lists.linux.dev>
Description:
		Read-only diagnostics for the common G16S/G17P firmware percent
		ceiling. Present only after registration with a qualified firmware
		layout. One key/value pair per line:

		requested_percent: 100 minus the thermal cooling state (0..100).
		published_percent: the percent synchronously stored in all three
		firmware mirrors, after composing the qualification backstop.
		applied_percent: unsupported; host stores have no acknowledgement.
		achieved_percent: unsupported; not inferred from a nominal OPP.
		qualification_backstop_percent: maximum allowed host publication.

		All numeric values are interface percentages, not watts, frequency
		or a proven achieved utilization. The qualification backstop cannot
		be released through this attribute. Firmware-reported achieved
		pstate, when available, is independently exposed in agx_stats and
		does not acknowledge a percent ceiling. J700 initialization is
		refused while its firmware allocation-relative layout is unknown;
		this attribute is consequently absent on that board.
